== Case text (Ask-CK ck.db zephyr_cases, read-only)
Case:          AWPTCM-T20358  (Approved)
Title:         Loopback between two ports on same switch
Objective (verbatim): When a switch port receives its own BPDU from the same edge port, it sets the port to the blocking state.
               When it no longer receives BPDUs, it sets the port to the forwarding state.
Precondition:  (empty)
Step 1 text (verbatim):
  - Connect the RSTP switch and a hub/switch.
  - Create a loop network switch.
  - Send broadcast traffic from IXIA
  - Confirm Port11 of RSTP switch. RSTP Port Role should be set to BackUp (Loopback Disabled) and State should set to Discarding.
  - Confirm backup port should not transmit traffic
Step 1 test data: (empty)
Step 1 expected (verbatim): Backup port should not forward any packet in this state.

== Plan (triage 10:0x: "in-test: RSTP on the x230 ... broadcast from eth1"; refined here)
RSTP switch = the x230 (RSTP enabled for the case). "Hub/switch" = the IE520 stack, STP disabled (bench standing state), via
the two x230<->stack links: x230 port1.0.3 <-> stack port1.0.17 (copper) and x230 port1.0.4 <-> stack port1.0.3 (SX fibre).
Safe order (never a loop without a blocking port):
  S1 x230 `spanning-tree rstp enable`; the two x230 ports stay in different VLANs (103 / 104), so no data loop exists.
  S2 stack port1.0.3 -> VLAN 103, so the stack bridges port1.0.17 <-> port1.0.3: the x230's BPDUs sent on port1.0.3 should
     come back on port1.0.4, which should go Backup / Discarding. GATE: S3 only if port1.0.4 reads Backup Discarding.
  S3 x230 port1.0.4 -> VLAN 103 (the loop), S4 x230 port1.0.5 (eth3) -> VLAN 103 and broadcast from eth3 (linerate.py),
     comparing x230 port1.0.3/1.0.4 output and stack port1.0.17/1.0.3 input counters, plus an inbound capture on eth3.
  Stack loop-protection (vlan-disable, 7 s, on port1.0.17 and port1.0.3) deliberately LEFT ON as a safety net: with a working
  Backup port the stack's loop-detect frames never return, so it cannot fire; if it did, that would itself show a leak.

