GATE FAILED: for 20 s (10 hello intervals of 2 s) x230 port1.0.4 stayed "Designated Forwarding": it never received the
  BPDU the x230 sends on port1.0.3. The IE520 stack, with spanning tree disabled, does not forward BPDUs between
  port1.0.17 and port1.0.3 (it terminates them), so it cannot act as the case's "hub/switch". Going on to S3 would have
  closed a real loop with no blocking port. S3 and S4 were NOT done.
Reverted immediately (19:16:3x): stack "interface port1.0.3" "switchport access vlan 104" -> show vlan brief:
103     VLAN0103         STATIC  ACTIVE  port1.0.17(u) 
104     VLAN0104         STATIC  ACTIVE  port1.0.3(u) 
Checked for a stack option to pass BPDUs (read-only qmark, work/qm-u5.out, qm2-u5.out, qm3-u5.out):
  config "no spanning-tree rstp enable ?" -> only "bridge-forward  put all ports of the bridge into forwarding state
  (default)" and <cr> (bridge-forward is already the default; it is about port states, not BPDU forwarding);
  config-if "spanning-tree ?" -> autoedge/edgeport/force-version/guard/hello-time/link-type/mst/path-cost/portfast/
  priority/restricted-role/restricted-tcn; "l2 ?" -> "% Unrecognized command" (no L2 protocol tunnelling on the IE520).
  So the stack cannot be made BPDU-transparent.

